DECK="embrace_protopia"; REV="t4"
INTRO="Forget Utopia. Ignore Dystopia. Embrace Protopia: Kult Kards for Tomorrow."
OUTRO="Answer with your paws. What can be improved today?"
L=[
 (1,"Ever notice how","The Open Notebook pictures the future as a page with room left on it, not a poster on a wall?",""),
 (2,"Room for what? Mistakes.","The Erasable Line draws the next step in pencil. Pencil means you expect to be wrong and stay anyway.",""),
 (3,"My grandmother swore by","The Ugly First Draft: make the first version bad on purpose. Bad is how you know it is real.",""),
 (4,"Real things are never done, says","The Next Pass. Improve it once, then leave it better and open.",""),
 (5,"Problem too big? Look for","The Fixable Thing, one broken thing close enough to touch.",""),
 (6,"Fix it this week, says","The Right-Sized Move, not a revolution you can only announce.",""),
 (7,"Will it trend? No.","The Boring Win: small fixes do not trend. They just hold.",""),
 (8,"But do the math with","The Compounding: one repair a week is fifty-two a year. Nobody clapped, and the place is different.",""),
 (9,"Itching to react? Take","The Held Breath, the one breath the feed is built to deny you.",""),
 (10,"Lower, says","The Lower Lung: breathe low enough to think. The nervous system votes with oxygen.",""),
 (11,"Bored already? Good.","The Boring Gap feels like falling behind. It is actually catching up to yourself.",""),
 (12,"Freedom, smallest size:","The Reclaimed Second. Take one second back, then another.",""),
 (13,"Need advice?","The Person Nearby: authority is overrated, proximity is underrated. Ask the one who actually does the thing.",""),
 (15,"Rumor has it","The Unimpressive Source is badly dressed and lives three doors down.",""),
 (16,"And what she knows","The Shared Skill passes hand to hand. It cannot be deplatformed.",""),
 (17,"Stop watching.","The Invitation: name a time, a place, a task.",""),
 (18,"Bring the neighbours, says","The Shared Hands: split a problem the way your ancestors raised a barn.",""),
 (19,"Awkward? Very.","The Awkward Start: go to the first small, clumsy gathering anyway. Clumsy is the entry fee.",""),
 (21,"When does the future start? In","The Available Hour: the next few hours. Start there.",""),
 (22,"Someday never ships.","The Done Thing trades one perfect someday for one finished today.",""),
 (25,"I once met","The Unknown Face: a possible ally with a different toolbox, not a threat.",""),
 (26,"We said hello. That's","The First Hello: most cooperation starts embarrassingly small.",""),
 (27,"Then he didn't answer.","The Risk of Being Soft-Blocked: your nervous system thinks that is death. It is not.",""),
 (28,"So I went first anyway.","The Widened Circle: every ally was a stranger until somebody did.",""),
 (29,"What if you swapped doom for","The Open Question? Run on huh, I wonder, instead of we are doomed or we are saved.",""),
 (30,"Even better,","The Cheap Experiment: framed as an experiment, wonder costs less than hope.",""),
 (31,"And when it fails?","The Wrong Answer: be wrong a lot. Curiosity treats that as data, not defeat.",""),
 (33,"Did you know","The Logged Observation writes down what you actually saw, not what the headline said you would see?",""),
 (34,"My diary says:","The Honest Denominator counts the whole thing, including the times it worked and nobody noticed.",""),
 (37,"This week,","The Made Thing: make something with your hands. Bread, a fix, a fence.",""),
 (39,"Too slow? Exactly.","The Slow Reward works at the speed of hands. That is not a bug, it is the medicine.",""),
 (41,"Want in?","The Small Opening: do not storm the front gate. Find the side door nobody guards.",""),
 (42,"Then try","The Pilot Move: a tiny version, low stakes, real feedback, no permission needed.",""),
 (43,"To a stuck system it looks like","The Quiet Sabotage: improvement often looks like mild disobedience.",""),
 (44,"Arguing? Build","The Proof of Concept. One beats a thousand arguments.",""),
 (45,"Here's the hard part:","The Surrendered Sure. Give up being certain. It is harder than giving up money.",""),
 (46,"Out of the bath, please.","The Comfort of Maybe trades the warm baths of hopeless and handled for the cold shower of it depends on us.",""),
 (47,"Is it ever finished? No.","The Ongoing Effort: the cost is showing up again next week.",""),
 (48,"And the bill?","The Worthwhile Bill: pay in certainty and comfort. Get back the wheel the other two decks took.",""),
 (49,"How do you know it's yours?","The Visible Seam: if you can see how it was made, you can remake it.",""),
 (51,"More than one way out? Then","The Plural Path: it is a future, not a funnel.",""),
 (53,"Look around, right now:","The Nearest Lever, the one thing within arm's reach.",""),
 (54,"Small print:","The One Percent. You do not need the whole future. You need today, one percent better.",""),
 (55,"And the applause?","The Quiet Start: nobody will clap. Start anyway. The clapping was never the point.",""),
 (56,"So, what now?","The Core Question: forget the brochure. Ignore the loop. Pick up the pencil.",""),
]
